Why: a host setting (CUA_DRIVER_WINDOW_CHANGE_REPORT_MS) for how long an action's result waits for a window change, so an embedding app whose agents read the window again after each action gets results back sooner while the focus-steal protection keeps its whole timeout.

Every action that opens nothing held its result for the 300 ms report
window. The existing CUA_DRIVER_WINDOW_CHANGE_TIMEOUT_MS can only shorten
that together with the protection behind it. This reads one more variable,
capped at the 300 ms default, used only for the report window; unset keeps
today's behaviour. Upstreamable as is.

